# Agent Cowork local/interview configuration template.
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and fill only the values you actually need.
# Keep real API keys out of commits. Placeholder values intentionally use dummy/sample words
# so `npm run check:secrets` can distinguish examples from leaked credentials.
#
# Env var naming: this file uses the current ACW_* prefix (Agent Cowork). Every host
# read site still accepts the legacy KCW_* name (and, for model vars, the older bare
# KIMI_* name) as a fallback during this compat window, so an existing `.env` written
# against older docs keeps working unchanged -- there is no need to migrate it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 0. Interview demo defaults
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web/MVP demo entry:
#   npm run demo:mvp
#   npm run start:mvp
# Desktop sidecar entry:
#   npm run start:tauri-host
#
# Keep HOST on loopback for normal demos. Binding 0.0.0.0 exposes the local
# file/tool API to the network and should be treated as a separate deployment task.
HOST=127.0.0.1
# Tauri sidecar uses 3017. Plain `npm start` falls back to 3001 when PORT is absent.
PORT=3017
# The host may only read/write under this root. Leave empty to use the current directory.
# TRUSTED_ROOT=C:\Users\Administrator\Desktop\agent cowork

# Security posture:
#   local_strict      local/offline first; external network tools are blocked and high-risk
#                     execution requires a network-isolated Docker/VM sandbox.
#   enterprise_hybrid local/customer gateway allowed; public cloud providers are blocked.
#   saas_opt_in       reserved controlled-hybrid posture. Public cloud execution still
#                     fails closed in this Internal Beta until approval-receipt consumption lands.
SECURITY_MODE=local_strict
# ACW_SECURITY_MODE=local_strict
# ACW_CUSTOMER_MODEL_GATEWAY_HOSTS=llm-gateway.corp,models.example.internal
#
# Confidential master switch (enterprise "air-gapped tier", see plan/08). When on, it
# force-locks securityMode=air_gap (cannot be weakened by any config/env), denies cloud
# model providers (local Ollama/LM Studio style providers keep working), blocks external
# network tools, drops ALL startup MCP servers (including the MASE memory bridge), and
# returns 403 for the whole OAuth connector surface. /api/selfcheck reports it.
# ACW_CONFIDENTIAL=1
#
# At-rest encryption for local content (conversations, run records, checkpoints, memory).
# A random data key (DEK) does the fast AES-256-GCM; the DEK is wrapped once by DPAPI (Windows)
# / an env-derived key and kept at <workspace>/.AgentCowork/security/at-rest.key. Reads always
# handle legacy plaintext transparently.
#
# Default policy is tier-bound (hardened, no flag needed):
#   - air_gap (incl. ACW_CONFIDENTIAL=1): ON and non-disableable (fail-closed).
#   - local_strict / enterprise_local: ON by default; set ACW_ENCRYPT_AT_REST=0 to opt out.
#   - local_demo / controlled_hybrid (standard): OFF by default; set ACW_ENCRYPT_AT_REST=1 to opt in.
# ACW_ENCRYPT_AT_REST=1   # force on for any tier
# ACW_ENCRYPT_AT_REST=0   # force off (ignored under air_gap)
#
# Data lifecycle (see plan/08): POST /api/security/data/purge-plan (read-only review),
# POST /api/security/data/purge {scope, confirm:true} (irreversible wipe, jailed to
# .AgentCowork; scopes: conversations|runs|memory|content|everything), and
# POST /api/security/data/retention {maxAgeDays} (delete run/conversation JSON older than N days).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Model provider: local OpenAI-compatible API (default)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ollama and LM Studio are the supported live-model path for this Internal Beta.
# Public-cloud provider entries remain discoverable in the catalog, but direct public-cloud
# execution fails closed until the approval-receipt consumer is implemented and accepted.
ACW_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai/local
# Generic model overrides (apply to whichever provider is selected above).
ACW_MODEL_API_KEY=
ACW_MODEL_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
ACW_MODEL=qwen2.5:0.5b
ACW_MODEL_API_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
ACW_MODEL_API_MAX_TOKENS=2048
# Optional request metadata/tuning. Leave unset unless the upstream provider asks for it.
# ACW_MODEL_USER_AGENT=agent-cowork-interview-demo
# ACW_MODEL_TEMPERATURE=0.2
#
# The kimi-api provider (Moonshot's real Kimi API) additionally accepts its own
# provider-specific credential aliases instead of ACW_MODEL_API_KEY/ACW_MODEL_BASE_URL:
# KIMI_API_KEY=
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
# KIMI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# MOONSHOT_BASE_URL=https://api.moonshot.ai/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Catalog-only public-cloud provider examples (execution unavailable in this beta)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The host normalizes provider/key/url/model in apps/host/src/engine/api-runner-config.ts.
# Do not enable these examples for a live demo: catalog discovery/configuration exists, but
# the governed request path deliberately refuses public-cloud egress without a consumable
# approval receipt. Customer-owned gateways must be allowlisted separately.
# ACW_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=dummy_anthropic_api_key_for_local_demo
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-demo
#
# JSON fallback catalog used by the model runner. Keep it one line in `.env`.
# ACW_MODEL_FALLBACKS=[{"provider":"kimi-api","model":"kimi-k2.7-code"},{"provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-sonnet-demo"}]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2b. Optional opencode-style provider_id/model_id presets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model selection follows opencode desktop's catalog-first shape. Public-cloud ids below are
# catalog/configuration entries only in this Internal Beta; local and allowlisted customer
# gateways are the executable paths.
#   provider_id/model_id
# Built-in OpenAI-compatible provider ids include:
#   kimi-api, deepseek, qwen-dashscope-cn, zai-glm, volcengine-ark,
#   baidu-qianfan, tencent-hunyuan, minimax, iflytek-spark,
#   siliconflow-cn, openai/local, lmstudio, custom-openai-compatible.
# Example:
# ACW_MODEL_PROVIDER=deepseek
# ACW_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash
# Or one full id when provider is omitted:
# ACW_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=dummy_deepseek_api_key_for_local_demo
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=dummy_dashscope_api_key_for_local_demo
# ZAI_API_KEY=dummy_zai_api_key_for_local_demo
# ARK_API_KEY=dummy_ark_api_key_for_local_demo
# QIANFAN_API_KEY=dummy_qianfan_api_key_for_local_demo
# HUNYUAN_API_KEY=dummy_hunyuan_api_key_for_local_demo
# MINIMAX_API_KEY=dummy_minimax_api_key_for_local_demo
# SPARK_API_KEY=dummy_spark_api_key_for_local_demo
# SILICONFLOW_API_KEY=dummy_siliconflow_api_key_for_local_demo
# Local OpenAI-compatible services do not require an API key:
# ACW_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai/local
# ACW_MODEL_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# ACW_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:7b

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2c. Automatic history compaction (context window aware)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The agent auto-compacts chat history before each model call. When the request
# does not pin an explicit maxContextTokens, the threshold adapts to the selected
# model's context window (see apps/host/src/engine/context/model-context-window.ts),
# using this input ratio to leave headroom for the model's output. Unknown models
# fall back to the compactor's conservative built-in default. Range 0.1-1.0.
# ACW_CONTEXT_INPUT_RATIO=0.75
#
# Local / BYO gateways (openai/local Ollama, lmstudio, custom-openai-compatible) do
# NOT get a guessed context window from the model name, because one local endpoint can
# serve any model at any num_ctx and over-guessing risks context overflow. Declare the
# real window in tokens here (e.g. an Ollama model started with a 8192 num_ctx). This
# also overrides the built-in window for cloud providers when set.
# ACW_MODEL_CONTEXT_WINDOW=8192
#
# Convergence knobs (reduce "always burns through all the steps"). Both default to the
# built-in behavior; set only to tune or disable.
#   ACW_STEP_NUDGE_RATIO: at this fraction of the step budget the loop injects one soft
#     "wrap up if you have enough" reminder. Default 0.7. Set 0 to disable the reminder.
#   ACW_TOOL_DISCIPLINE: set 0/off to drop the tool-use discipline block from the system
#     prompt (batch parallel calls, stop when done, don't repeat). Default on.
# ACW_STEP_NUDGE_RATIO=0.7
# ACW_TOOL_DISCIPLINE=1
#   ACW_MAX_AUTO_CONTINUE: when one message's task is too big and hits the per-turn step
#     budget while still working, auto-continue this many extra windows so it finishes in
#     one go. Hard cap on tool rounds = maxSteps*(1+this). Budget/timeout/loop guards still
#     apply. Default 2 (up to 3 windows). Set 0 to disable auto-continue.
# ACW_MAX_AUTO_CONTINUE=2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Auth and request boundary
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Require a valid local session/JWT on every /api route. Keep true for anything
# beyond isolated tests; tests set their own environment in scripts/test-setup.ts.
ACW_REQUIRE_AUTH=true
# Register/guest enrollment is closed by default. To create exactly one initial
# identity, set a random value of at least 32 characters locally, send it once in
# x-acw-enrollment-token (legacy clients may still send x-kcw-enrollment-token), then
# remove it and restart the host before any later enrollment.
# ACW_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN=sample_random_one_time_enrollment_capability_32_chars
# Only set a JWT secret for stateless multi-instance demos. Empty means local opaque sessions.
ACW_JWT_SECRET=
# Do not trust x-tenant-id/x-user-id from clients unless a trusted reverse proxy strips
# attacker-supplied identity headers before requests reach the host.
ACW_TRUST_IDENTITY_HEADERS=false
# Host header validation blocks DNS-rebinding style access. Keep true for local demos.
ACW_VALIDATE_HOST=true
# Persist login/session state to `.AgentCowork/auth.sqlite`. Set false only for tests.
ACW_AUTH_PERSIST=true
# ACW_AUTH_DB=C:\Users\Administrator\AppData\Roaming\AgentCowork\auth.sqlite
# Host-global writes (model config, MCP registry, skill enabled state, purge, retention)
# require an exact tenantId+userId tuple from the server-derived request identity. When
# unset, only tenant_local/user_local is allowed. Setting this JSON array replaces that
# default; [] denies every identity. Missing/extra fields, user-only entries, invalid JSON,
# duplicate tuples, or invalid ids make host startup fail closed.
# ACW_GLOBAL_MUTATION_ADMINS=[{"tenantId":"tenant_ops","userId":"user_admin"}]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Storage backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# sqlite: default single-file durable local state; file: legacy/local diagnostics; postgres: multi-instance demo.
ACW_STORE=sqlite
# ACW_STORE=file
# ACW_SQLITE_PATH=C:\Users\Administrator\AppData\Roaming\AgentCowork\state.sqlite
#
# Postgres requires applying apps/host/src/storage/migrations-postgres/0001_init.sql first.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://agent_cowork:sample_password@127.0.0.1:5432/agent_cowork
# PGPOOL_MAX=20

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Sandbox and local runtimes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# auto: prefer Docker with a configured local image; otherwise fall back to local subprocess
# and report that network isolation is not guaranteed.
ACW_SANDBOX_BACKEND=auto
# Local/WSL execution has no workspace or OS isolation and is denied by default.
# Enabling this host capability still requires each request to set unrestrictedHostExecution=true.
# ACW_ALLOW_UNRESTRICTED_HOST_EXECUTION=false
# ACW_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE=agent-cowork-sandbox:local
# Used only by the real Docker network-isolation smoke:
# ACW_SANDBOX_REAL_DOCKER_IMAGE=postgres:16-alpine
#
# Bundled/portable runtime overrides. These are useful for installed-build demos.
# ACW_NODE_EXE=C:\Tools\node\node.exe
# ACW_NODE_HOME=C:\Tools\node
# ACW_EMBEDDED_PYTHON=C:\Tools\python\python.exe
# ACW_PYTHON_HOME=C:\Tools\python
# ACW_MINGIT_HOME=C:\Tools\mingit
# ACW_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE=C:\Program Files\Google\Chrome\Application\chrome.exe
# ACW_PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_HOME=C:\Users\Administrator\AppData\Local\ms-playwright
# ACW_WEBVIEW2_MODE=runtime
# ACW_VC_RUNTIME_INSTALLED=1
# ACW_CJK_FONT=C:\Windows\Fonts\msyh.ttc
# ACW_PANDOC_EXE=C:\Tools\pandoc\pandoc.exe
# ACW_TESSERACT_HOME=C:\Tools\tesseract
# ACW_DATA_SCIENCE_HOME=C:\Tools\data-science

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Rate limits, concurrency, and logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ACW_RATE_PER_SEC=50
ACW_RATE_BURST=100
ACW_MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=64
ACW_MAX_RUNS_PER_TENANT=8
ACW_LOG_MAX_BYTES=8388608
ACW_LOG_MAX_FILES=3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6b. Optional ONLYOFFICE Document Server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Disabled by default. See docs/onlyoffice-document-server.md and
# deploy/onlyoffice/docker-compose.yml. Keep the real shared secret only in `.env`.
ACW_ONLYOFFICE_ENABLED=false
# Browser-facing Document Server URL (the bundled Compose maps it to loopback port 8082).
# ACW_ONLYOFFICE_DOCUMENT_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8082
# URL Document Server uses to call this host. Docker Desktop resolves this name to Windows.
# ACW_ONLYOFFICE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:3017
# Must exactly match ONLYOFFICE_JWT_SECRET in deploy/onlyoffice/.env.
ACW_ONLYOFFICE_JWT_SECRET=
ACW_ONLYOFFICE_JWT_HEADER=Authorization
# ACW_ONLYOFFICE_SESSION_TTL_MS=7200000
# ACW_ONLYOFFICE_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
# ACW_ONLYOFFICE_MAX_FILE_BYTES=104857600

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Credentials and connectors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App home stores sessions, credentials, and other host-owned state. The Windows
# default is `%APPDATA%\AgentCowork`; override only for portable or test installs.
# AGENT_COWORK_HOME=C:\Users\Administrator\AppData\Roaming\AgentCowork
#
# Credential store secrets are encrypted with DPAPI on Windows when available. ACW_CREDENTIAL_KEY
# is only for non-Windows or deterministic test/demo stores; do not commit a real value.
# ACW_CREDENTIAL_STORE=C:\Users\Administrator\AppData\Roaming\AgentCowork\credentials.json
# ACW_CREDENTIAL_KEY=sample_credential_key_min_32_chars_for_demo
#
# GitHub connector uses OAuth device flow. It needs a public client id, not a client secret.
# ACW_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=sample_github_oauth_client_id

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Optional report/output locations for smoke scripts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are useful when you want interview evidence in a separate folder.
# MVP_RUNTIME_FILE=build/mvp-runtime.json
# REACT_CONNECTORS_REPORT_DIR=reports/react-connectors
# REACT_SCROLL_REPORT_DIR=reports/react-scroll
# REACT_ARTIFACTS_REPORT_DIR=reports/react-artifacts
# PLAN_LOOP_REPORT_DIR=reports/plan-closed-loop
# WINDOWS_PATHS_REPORT_DIR=reports/windows-paths

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. Optional long-term memory backend (MASE MCP)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When enabled, the host auto-connects a MASE memory MCP server on startup and uses it
# as an automatic memory backend: each turn recalls relevant history/facts into context
# and writes the user+assistant turn back (see apps/host/src/memory/mase-bridge.ts).
# Disabled by default; when unset the whole bridge is a no-op and built-in file memory is used.
#
# Safety boundaries already enforced by the bridge:
#   - Credential/secret-bearing content is classified (security/data-classifier) and skipped
#     before any write leaves the machine (same DLP guard as built-in memory).
#   - Recall and write-back both respect the workspace memory switch (pause/incognito/disabled
#     in .AgentCowork/memory-settings.json), so the UI toggle really stops live memory.
#
# Enable both of the next two to turn it on:
# MASE_MCP_ENABLED=1
# MASE_REPO=C:\Path\To\mase-repo
# Optional overrides (defaults derive from MASE_REPO):
# MASE_CONFIG_PATH=C:\Path\To\mase-repo\config.json
# Point memory storage at a writable dir (avoids sandbox-read-only drives):
# MASE_MEMORY_DIR=C:\Users\Administrator\AppData\Roaming\AgentCowork\mase-memory
